{"name":"Sun Kiss","hex":"#eacdb7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sun","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Sundanese."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The star that is closest to the Earth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun"},{"term":"kiss","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To touch with the lips or press the lips against, usually to show love or affection or passion, or as part of a greeting.","To (cause to) touch lightly or slightly; to come into contact."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A touch with the lips, usually to express love or affection, or as a greeting.","An 'X' mark placed at the end of a letter or other type of message, signifying the bestowal of a kiss from the sender to the receiver."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kiss"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sun Kiss (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Sun Kiss\" is a song recorded by South Korean girl group Tuide for their debut extended play (EP) Tune & Play. It was released as the lead single by ABD on August 24, 2026."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun_Kiss_(song)"},{"title":"Jeanneau","blocks":[{"text":"Jeanneau is a French boatyard in Les Herbiers, in the Vendée département, which has produced yachts since 1957. It was founded by Henri Jeanneau, a hardware store owner, who began by producing power boats."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bb/Jeanneau_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeanneau"},{"title":"Sun","blocks":[{"text":"The Sun is the star located at the centre of the Solar System. It is a massive sphere of hot plasma, heated to incandescence by nuclear fusion reactions in its core, radiating the energy from its surface mainly as visible light and infrared radiation, with 10% at ultraviolet energies. It is the main source of energy for life on Earth. The Sun has been an object of veneration in many cultures and a central subject of astronomical research since antiquity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun"},{"title":"Kiss","blocks":[{"text":"A kiss is the touching or pressing of one's lips against another person, animal, or object. The cultural connotations associated with kissing vary significantly between different societies and contexts. Depending on the culture and circumstances, a kiss can express a wide range of emotions, such as love, passion, romance, sexual attraction, sexual arousal, affection, respect, a wish for peace or good luck, as well as numerous other meanings. In some situations, kissing takes on the function of a greeting or a ritual, formal, or symbolic gesture indicating religious devotion, institutional respect, or an act of sacramental nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg/330px-Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiss"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Jeanneau_Sun_Odyssey_349_sailboat_French_Kiss_2351.jpg/500px-Jeanneau_Sun_Odyssey_349_sailboat_French_Kiss_2351.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Jeanneau_Sun_Odyssey_349_sailboat_French_Kiss_2351.jpg/1280px-Jeanneau_Sun_Odyssey_349_sailboat_French_Kiss_2351.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Jeanneau_Sun_Odyssey_349_sailboat_French_Kiss_2351.jpg/500px-Jeanneau_Sun_Odyssey_349_sailboat_French_Kiss_2351.jpg?utm_sou